  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Prove the following logarithm laws, using the proof of Theorem 1 as a guide:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\log_b\\frac{x}{y}=\\log_b x-\\log_b y$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Let $m=\\log_b x$ and $n=\\log_b y$. Then $\\frac{x}{y}=b^{m-n}$, so $\\log_b(\\frac{x}{y})=m-n=\\log_b x-\\log_b y$.",
          "worked": "For $b>0$, $b\\ne1$ and $x,y>0$, let $m=\\log_b x$ and $n=\\log_b y$. Then $x=b^m$ and $y=b^n$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{y}&=\\frac{b^m}{b^n}\\\\\\frac{x}{y}&=b^{m-n}.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the definition of a logarithm,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_b\\frac{x}{y}&=m-n\\\\\\log_b\\frac{x}{y}&=\\log_b x-\\log_b y.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      },
      {
        "id": "p8-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\log_b x^c=c\\log_b x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Let $m=\\log_b x$. Then $x^c=b^{mc}$, so $\\log_b x^c=mc=c\\log_b x$.",
          "worked": "For $b>0$, $b\\ne1$ and $x>0$, let $m=\\log_b x$. Then $x=b^m$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^c&=(b^m)^c\\\\x^c&=b^{mc}.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the definition of a logarithm,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_b x^c&=mc\\\\\\log_b x^c&=c\\log_b x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      }
    ]
  },
